# Requests for the main app (npm run dev). VS Code "REST Client" extension.
# After creating a prompt, copy its id into @id below.

@base = http://localhost:3000
@id = paste-an-id-here

### Create as alice (expect 201)
POST {{base}}/api/prompts
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: alice

{
  "title": "Summarise a paper",
  "content": "Summarise the following paper in 5 bullet points: <paper>",
  "tags": ["summarisation", "research"]
}

### Create — invalid (expect 400 with details for title and content)
POST {{base}}/api/prompts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "ab", "content": "short" }

### Create — try to set server-owned fields (they must be ignored)
POST {{base}}/api/prompts
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: alice

{ "title": "Sneaky", "content": "Trying to set my own id and version", "id": "hacked", "version": 99, "createdBy": "admin" }

### List (page 1, 5 per page)
GET {{base}}/api/prompts?page=1&limit=5

### List — invalid page (expect 400)
GET {{base}}/api/prompts?page=0

### Get one
GET {{base}}/api/prompts/{{id}}

### Get one — not found (expect 404)
GET {{base}}/api/prompts/does-not-exist

### Update as owner — content change bumps version
PATCH {{base}}/api/prompts/{{id}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: alice

{ "content": "Summarise the following paper in 3 bullet points: <paper>" }

### Update as someone else (expect 403)
PATCH {{base}}/api/prompts/{{id}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: bob

{ "title": "Hacked by bob" }

### Delete as owner (expect 204), run it twice: what does the second call return?
DELETE {{base}}/api/prompts/{{id}}
x-user-id: alice
